# pi (earendil-works/pi) as a harness in a Shards microVM: the Agentfile kiln ships for it (plan
# 01a1cd8e862e7169a074db3d5fa33f3d, step 28; plan 01a1ce705e62732b83f16295d74ee263, research
# 01a1ce705e62732b86d3534d788ae242, f1-f30). kiln drives pi in its RPC mode (Kind `pi`,
# crates/kiln/src/harness/pi.rs; f13, f14). Its build context is what `kiln agentfiles context pi DIR`
# writes: this file, and for each platform pi-<arch>/ with harness.json, pi's release tarball unpacked
# whole at its root less its pi/ (pi reads its package files beside its executable, f11), and bin/rg
# and bin/fd, each file checked against pin.json. It holds no credential: a person's sign-in stays on
# their own volume (below).

# pi's Linux builds are Bun executables for glibc: they need glibc's loader and link only libc,
# libpthread, libdl and libm, at GLIBC_2.17 at most (f9). Any base of glibc 2.17 or later runs them
# with no RUN; this default, the digest pin.sh read (pin.json's base), is Debian trixie with glibc
# 2.41. pi publishes no musl build, so there is no libc variant, and a musl base (Alpine) can't start
# pi (f10).
ARG BASE=buildpack-deps:trixie-scm@sha256:4f34e1d673fdb65371de9f88bdd32c4e30152fe692b35604aef5c0b3c0e6da10
FROM ${BASE}

# pi's own build for the platform being built (TARGETARCH, f21). Its bin/ holds the ripgrep and fd
# builds pi's grep and find tools would otherwise download, unpinned, at first use: shards-init puts
# it on pi's PATH, where pi finds them, so pi downloads nothing (f16, f17, f18).
ARG TARGETARCH
HARNESS pi FROM ./pi-${TARGETARCH}

# Its network, every part named (default deny; Shards D236, destinations by name): a network for this
# harness alone, which it joins with no flow to any member, and TCP out to the hosts below alone, by
# name, through the network's boundary (--egress) and the microVM's (EXPOSE ... AS egress). Each name
# resolves for it through the agents' resolver, and no other does. Nothing comes in; no other host,
# port or protocol goes out. 443 is HTTPS's port (RFC 9110 4.2.2). Each host is cited to its vendor's own
# documentation, or, where that names a wildcard or nothing, to the vendor's own source or build, in its
# harness's record's "Hosts by name" (kiln plan 01a1cd8e862e7169a074db3d5fa33f3d, step 18, part 4):
# docs/research/s28-pi-agentfile/README.md and its evidence/hosts/hosts.tsv: every provider pi 1.5.2's own build
# reaches at a fixed public host (its providers docs list them), with the sign-in hosts of those it signs in to
# itself, and pi.dev, its catalog's refreshes. Not granted: a provider whose resource or region places its host
# (Azure, Bedrock, Vertex AI); a local server or an endpoint the person gives in models.json (a local Ollama, a
# regional OpenRouter). Each of those needs an Agentfile of your own, made from this one.
# Each host is cited to its provider's own API docs and to the harness's own source, or to that source alone where
# no page of the provider's own docs names it (ROOT's call of 2026-11-13, the person's bar: zero breaks against
# today); kiln's launch is to keep only the session's own provider's hosts (plan step 17). Each host, by its provider:
#   ai-gateway.vercel.sh (Vercel AI Gateway), api.ant-ling.com (Ant Ling), api.anthropic.com (Anthropic),
#   api.cerebras.ai (Cerebras), api.cloudflare.com (Cloudflare Workers AI), api.deepseek.com (DeepSeek),
#   api.fireworks.ai (Fireworks), api.github.com (GitHub Copilot token), api.groq.com (Groq),
#   api.individual.githubcopilot.com (GitHub Copilot), api.kimi.com (Kimi For Coding), api.meta.ai (Meta),
#   api.minimax.io (MiniMax), api.minimaxi.com (MiniMax (China)), api.mistral.ai (Mistral), api.moonshot.ai
#   (Moonshot AI (Global)), api.moonshot.cn (Moonshot AI (China)), api.openai.com (OpenAI), api.together.ai
#   (Together AI), api.typesafe.ai (TypeSafe), api.x.ai (xAI), api.xiaomimimo.com (Xiaomi MiMo), api.z.ai (ZAI
#   Coding Plan (Global)), auth.kimi.com (Kimi For Coding sign-in), auth.meta.com (Meta sign-in), auth.openai.com
#   (OpenAI ChatGPT sign-in), auth.x.ai (xAI sign-in), chatgpt.com (OpenAI ChatGPT (Codex)),
#   gateway.ai.cloudflare.com (Cloudflare AI Gateway), generativelanguage.googleapis.com (Google Gemini), github.com
#   (GitHub Copilot device sign-in), inference.baseten.co (Baseten), integrate.api.nvidia.com (NVIDIA NIM),
#   open.bigmodel.cn (ZAI Coding Plan (China)), opencode.ai (OpenCode Zen and Go), openrouter.ai (OpenRouter),
#   pi.dev (pi's catalog overlays (models.md)), platform.claude.com (Anthropic sign-in (token exchange and
#   refresh)), radius.pi.dev (Radius), router.huggingface.co (Hugging Face), token-plan-ams.xiaomimimo.com (Xiaomi
#   MiMo Token Plan (Amsterdam)), token-plan-cn.xiaomimimo.com (Xiaomi MiMo Token Plan (China)),
#   token-plan-sgp.xiaomimimo.com (Xiaomi MiMo Token Plan (Singapore)), token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com
#   (Qwen Token Plan and Individual), token-plan.cn-beijing.maas.aliyuncs.com (Qwen Token Plan (China) and
#   Individual (China)).
# Pi takes no MCP server from kiln, and no Agentfile of kiln's grants anything for kiln's MCP.
NETWORK --egress=ai-gateway.vercel.sh:443 --egress=api.ant-ling.com:443 --egress=api.anthropic.com:443 --egress=api.cerebras.ai:443 --egress=api.cloudflare.com:443 --egress=api.deepseek.com:443 --egress=api.fireworks.ai:443 --egress=api.github.com:443 --egress=api.groq.com:443 --egress=api.individual.githubcopilot.com:443 --egress=api.kimi.com:443 --egress=api.meta.ai:443 --egress=api.minimax.io:443 --egress=api.minimaxi.com:443 --egress=api.mistral.ai:443 --egress=api.moonshot.ai:443 --egress=api.moonshot.cn:443 --egress=api.openai.com:443 --egress=api.together.ai:443 --egress=api.typesafe.ai:443 --egress=api.x.ai:443 --egress=api.xiaomimimo.com:443 --egress=api.z.ai:443 --egress=auth.kimi.com:443 --egress=auth.meta.com:443 --egress=auth.openai.com:443 --egress=auth.x.ai:443 --egress=chatgpt.com:443 --egress=gateway.ai.cloudflare.com:443 --egress=generativelanguage.googleapis.com:443 --egress=github.com:443 --egress=inference.baseten.co:443 --egress=integrate.api.nvidia.com:443 --egress=open.bigmodel.cn:443 --egress=opencode.ai:443 --egress=openrouter.ai:443 --egress=pi.dev:443 --egress=platform.claude.com:443 --egress=radius.pi.dev:443 --egress=router.huggingface.co:443 --egress=token-plan-ams.xiaomimimo.com:443 --egress=token-plan-cn.xiaomimimo.com:443 --egress=token-plan-sgp.xiaomimimo.com:443 --egress=token-plan.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com:443 --egress=token-plan.cn-beijing.maas.aliyuncs.com:443 provider FOR pi
EXPOSE --harnesses=pi 443/tcp AS egress FOR provider
CONNECT pi WITH pi ON provider

# Its project is plugged in as it starts, at the path it has on the machine (Shards D235), so kiln
# reads its diffs, HEAD and checkpoints at that same path, and no volume holds it. Its HOME is the
# person's volume, whole: harness.json sets HOME=/home/pi, kiln's one rule for every harness it
# ships (step 18). A harness sees its image read-only, with its own /tmp scratch, so a HOME that is
# writable and kept from run to run is a volume, and what the programs it runs keep in a home (a
# .gitconfig, a tool's sign-in) is kept with it. pi keeps its sign-in (auth.json), settings, models
# and sessions in PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR beneath it (f15, f22).
# harness.json keeps caches that follow XDG's rule on the scratch (XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/.cache),
# where they were before its HOME moved onto the volume.
# HOME in run.env needs a shards at or after 997f4e47e (v0.8.0 and later), where run.env replaces
# init's HOME=/tmp. The volume is the harness's alone, and outside /tmp, which the scratch covers.
VOLUME --target-kind=harness /home/pi FOR pi
